<title>SIERRA LEONE: GOVERNMENT LIST. [CORRECTED 09:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST. [CORRECTED 09:50 GMT]</headline>
<text>
<p>SIERRA LEONE GOVERNMENT LIST (970526)</p>
<p>(Corrects surname of new leader to Koromah from Korma.)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> * 26 May 97 - Army Major Johnny Paul Koromah declared	 *</p>
<p> *		 himself head of state after the previous day's*</p>
<p> *		   coup.						   *</p>
<p> * 25 May 97 - Soldiers in Sierra Leone ousted the civilian  *</p>
<p> *		 government and President Ahmad Tejan Kabbah   *</p>
<p> *		 flew into exile in Guinea. The army seized    *</p>
<p> *		 parliament and government offices .	     *</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Head of State (From 26 May 97)............Johnny Paul KOROMAH</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>OUTGOING GOVERNMENT (Reshuffled 21 Nov 96)</p>
<p> President (Sworn in 29 Mar 96)...........Ahmad TEJAN KABBAH**</p>
<p>							  (**See NOTE Above)</p>
<p> Vice President...................................Albert DEMBY</p>
<p>			    - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS</p>
<p> Agriculture, Forestry &amp; Environment................Harry WILL</p>
<p> Development &amp; Economic Planning................Nat WELLINGTON</p>
<p> Education.........................................Alpha WURIE</p>
<p> Employment &amp; Industrial Relations.............Mohamed GASSAMA</p>
<p> Finance........................................Thaimu BANGURA</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs...............................Shirley GBUJAMA</p>
<p> Gender &amp; Children's Affairs........................Amy SMYTHE</p>
<p> Health &amp; Sanitation.............................Mohamed TURAY</p>
<p> Information &amp; Broadcasting.....................Thorlu BANGURA</p>
<p> Internal Affairs..............................Kemoh SALIA-BAO</p>
<p> Justice, Attorney General......................Solomon BEREWA</p>
<p> Labour, Social Welfare, Youth &amp; Sports...........Sheku SACCOH</p>
<p> Lands, Housing, Town &amp; Country Planning...........John KARIMU</p>
<p> Local Government &amp; Community Development...........David QUEE</p>
<p> Marine Resources..............................Lawrence KAMARA</p>
<p> Mineral Resources..............................Prince HARDING</p>
<p> National Reconstruction, Resettlement</p>
<p>    &amp; Rehabilitation.............................Momodu YILLAH</p>
<p> Parliamentary &amp; Political Affairs..............Abu Aih KOROMA</p>
<p> Presidential &amp; Public Service...................Momodu KOROMA</p>
<p> Tourism &amp; Culture.............................Yembeh MANSARAY</p>
<p> Transport, Communication &amp; Environment..Sulaiman TEJAN JALLOH</p>
<p> Trade, Industry &amp; State Enterprises.......George Banda THOMAS</p>
<p> Works, Energy &amp; power..........................Emmanuel GRANT</p>
<p>			     - - - - - -</p>
<p> Permanent representative to the U.N., special envoy &amp;</p>
<p>    adviser to the president.......................James JONAH</p>
<p>			     - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor............................Steve SWARAY</p>
<p>			     - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			 (End Government List)</p>
</text>
